Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:40:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] WIP: fuzz-smoke self-test, per-target runs; lengths and
 verdicts in one place

scripts/fuzz-smoke.sh --self-test proves, with no nightly or
cargo-fuzz, what the -max_len finding was about: every capped target is
a real target, its length reaches past its cap and is what the run
passes, and its boundary inputs are exactly the cap and one byte more;
and that a failure is called a finding only with a reproducer. The
fuzz-smoke job and make fuzz-lint run it first. Named targets narrow a
run, to reproduce one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ENZSCiAud5Vs29ugEacpyR
